= Michael Heseltine

Self-made publishing millionaire, conference star and, in his own view, a future Prime Minister. Labour MPs call him Tarzan since he seized the Commons mace in 1976.

- @conference
- @regeneration
- @minis
- @root: Return

@conference
title: A barnstorming conference speech
subtitle: The activists are thrilled. Your own rating suffers a little from the comparison.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; resources += 1; c1_con += 2*(1-dissent); c2_con += 1*(1-dissent); thatcher_rating -= 1; loyalist_dissent -= 3

Heseltine brings the conference hall to its feet. You clap along with everyone else.

@regeneration
title: Urban regeneration
view-if: con_in_government = 1
subtitle: -1 budget. The inner cities and the wets approve.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; budget -= 1; de_con += 2*(1-dissent); wet_dissent -= 5; dry_dissent += 3

Heseltine sends task forces of civil servants and businessmen into the worst inner-city estates, and promises a garden festival for Liverpool.

@minis
title: Cut the civil service
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and minis = 0
subtitle: +1 budget. The dries are impressed despite themselves.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; minis = 1; budget += 1; dry_dissent -= 3; union_power -= 1

Heseltine installs a management information system at the Department of the Environment and cuts its staff by more than a quarter. He suggests every department should do the same. Most ministers hope you won't ask them.
